IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`

-- Section 207: effective dates. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- These are not commencement machinery in the Guide's sense: they decide which weeks the Act
-- reaches (an extended benefit period cannot begin before 1 January 1972, section 204 applies to
-- weeks after 31 December 1971, section 3304(a)(11) of the Internal Revenue Code binds a State
-- law only from the dates in subsection (c)). The dates themselves are defined once, in
-- euca-shared, with the quotations that give them.
-- Section 206 (which amended section 3304(a) of the Internal Revenue Code) is not encoded:
-- it is an amendment of another instrument (see NOTES.md, coverage table).
-- out of text: section 3304(a)(11) of the Internal Revenue Code (the requirement that a State
-- law provide extended compensation, s 207(c)).

§ `Section 207: effective dates`

§§ `207(a)(1) and (b)(1): when an extended benefit period may begin`

-- src:137 | in applying section 203, no extended benefit period may begin with a week beginning before January 1, 1972
-- src:140 | such State law may also provide that an extended benefit period may begin with a week established pursuant to such law which begins earlier than January 1, 1972, but not earlier than 60 days after the date of the enactment of this Act
@ref s 207(a)(1) and (b)(1) (src:137 src:140)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      `a State law approved under section 3304(a)(11) provides that an extended benefit period may begin with the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an extended benefit period may begin with the week` week `a State law approved under section 3304(a)(11) provides that an extended benefit period may begin with the week` MEANS
        week AT LEAST `1 January 1972`
    OR  (   `a State law approved under section 3304(a)(11) provides that an extended benefit period may begin with the week`
        AND week AT LEAST `60 days after the date this title was enacted`)

§§ `207(b)(2): a period that begins before 1 January 1972`

-- src:141 | “(2) For purposes of paragraph (1) with respect to weeks beginning before January 1, 1972, the extended benefit period for the State shall be determined under section 203(a) solely by reference to the State ‘on’ indicator and the State ‘off’ indicator.
@ref s 207(b)(2) (src:141)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the extended benefit period is determined solely by the State on and off indicators` week MEANS
    week LESS THAN `1 January 1972`

§§ `207(a)(2) and (b)(3): when section 204 applies`

-- src:138 | section 204 shall apply only with respect to weeks of unemployment beginning after December 31, 1971
-- src:142 | In the case of a State law containing a provision described in paragraph (1), section 204 shall also apply with respect to weeks of unemployment in extended benefit periods determined pursuant to paragraph (1)
@ref s 207(a)(2) and (b)(3) (src:138 src:142)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      `the week is in an extended benefit period determined under a State law provision described in section 207(b)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 204 applies to the week of unemployment` week `the week is in an extended benefit period determined under a State law provision described in section 207(b)(1)` MEANS
        week GREATER THAN `31 December 1971`
    OR  `the week is in an extended benefit period determined under a State law provision described in section 207(b)(1)`

§§ `207(c): when section 3304(a)(11) of the Internal Revenue Code binds a State law`

-- Subsection (c) says when the requirement is NOT a requirement; this rule is the converse.
-- src:143 | “(c) Section 3304(a)(11) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 (as added by section 206) shall not be a requirement for the State law of any State—
-- src:144 | “(1) in the case of any State the legislature of which does not meet in a regular session which closes during the calendar year 1971, with respect to any week of unemployment which begins prior to July 1, 1972; or
-- src:145 | “(2) in the case of any other State, with respect to any week of unemployment which begins prior to January 1, 1972.
@ref s 207(c)(1) and (2) (src:143-145)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      `the legislature of the State does not meet in a regular session which closes during the calendar year 1971` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3304(a)(11) of the Internal Revenue Code is a requirement for the State law for the week` week `the legislature of the State does not meet in a regular session which closes during the calendar year 1971` MEANS
    IF `the legislature of the State does not meet in a regular session which closes during the calendar year 1971`
    THEN week AT LEAST `1 July 1972`
    ELSE week AT LEAST `1 January 1972`
